          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is oil-based or water-based asphalt sealer better?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For most homeowners, water-based (emulsion) sealers are the right choice — they are lower odor, environmentally safer, easier to clean up, and legal everywhere. Oil-based rejuvenators are only superior in the specific case of very dry, aged asphalt where you need to restore the original binder chemistry. For a full breakdown, see our oil-based vs. water-based driveway sealer comparison.",
          },
